# Milestones and documentation

## Workflow

1. Write Plan sections in `docs/milestones/M<N>-<slug>.md` first.
2. Wait for explicit user **approved** before coding that milestone.
3. After implementation:
   - In **chat**: highlight review-worthy code (citations), explain what changed and why.
   - In **docs**: fill Results, append `LEARNING_LOG.md`, update `docs/architecture.md` if topology changed.
4. Commit + push, then do not mark Done until the close-out checklist passes.

## Required sections in every milestone file

- Status, Goal, Why this milestone, Concepts introduced
- Design decisions & alternatives considered
- **Architecture graph (planned)** — Mermaid; freeze after approval
- Tasks, Demo / acceptance criteria
- **Results** with all of: What we did; Commands & how to reproduce; **As-built graph** (Mermaid) + delta vs planned; Why this approach; Deviations; Pitfalls & aha moments; Open questions / next dig

Full template copy lives in `docs/milestones/M0-environment.md` (reuse structure for later milestones).

## Graphs (mandatory)

- Plan graph before approval; Results as-built graph after coding (or note "unchanged").
- From M2+: include LangGraph node/edge topology (Mermaid; optional `draw_mermaid()` paste).
- Chat diagrams are ephemeral — copy into the milestone file.
- `docs/architecture.md` = current state only; milestone files = history.

## Close-out checklist

- Plan approved before coding
- Implementation landed
- Chat review handover: highlighted code + what/why explained
- Results complete in the milestone file (commands + why + graphs)
- LEARNING_LOG.md entry added
- architecture.md updated if needed
- Changes committed (English message) and pushed to GitHub
- Stop and wait for next approval

## Simplifications

Label teaching shortcuts as **simplification** and note what production would still need.
